{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"KILL SWITCH EXECUTED END-TO-END, POST-CUTOVER, WITH A REAL VOTE ON THE ANTHROPIC PATH AND THE CUTOVER RE-APPLIED. This is the criterion's hardest clause — it demands proof the lever has a WORKING CREDENTIAL, not merely that the config flipped — and it is now met by observation.\n\nTHE COMMANDS, exactly as run on the box (SSM), matching the runbook's fast path:\n  00:22:41Z  systemctl stop rebar-autodeploy.timer            -> autodeploy_timer=stopped, is-active=inactive\n             cp -a docker-compose.yml /tmp/docker-compose.yml.eb6e-backup\n             sed -i '/REBAR_LLM_FRONTIER_MODEL:/d;/REBAR_LLM_STANDARD_MODEL:/d;/REBAR_LLM_TRIVIAL_MODEL:/d' docker-compose.yml\n             -> slot lines remaining in file: 0\n             docker compose up -d --force-recreate review-bot  -> Recreated / Started\n             docker compose exec review-bot env | grep REBAR_LLM_<CLASS>_MODEL -> 'no class-slot overrides set'\n             rebar's own resolution in the container:\n                 frontier -> anthropic:claude-opus-4-8\n                 standard -> anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\n                 trivial  -> anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5\n\nWHY I PAUSED AUTODEPLOY, since it is an extra step the criterion does not name. The runbook entry landed in 1326 states the on-box edit is TRANSIENT: /opt/rebar is an rsync'd copy of main and infra/compose/docker-compose.yml is in autodeploy's BOT_PATHS, so the next main advance touching a bot path silently restores the Bedrock lines. A review takes roughly eight minutes end to end while autodeploy ticks every two, so without pausing the timer the lever would have been reverted mid-review and no Anthropic vote could have been produced. Stopping the timer for the duration is therefore what makes the criterion TESTABLE rather than a shortcut around it. The timer was restarted as part of the re-apply, verified is-active=active.\n\nTHE CREDENTIAL WORKS — six real calls on the DIRECT ANTHROPIC path, from the usage log, after the lever:\n    00:24:35  anthropic:claude-opus-4-8    in=230234  cache_read=200570  code-review-base\n    00:26:07  anthropic:claude-opus-4-8    in=392830  cache_read=335859  code-review-tests\n    00:26:53  anthropic:claude-opus-4-8    in=117599  cache_read=89366   code-review-scope-intent\n    00:26:57  anthropic:claude-opus-4-8    in=7133    cache_read=0       code-review-project-review-phase-boundaries\n    00:27:49  anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6  in=76506   cache_read=61982   code-review-verify\n    00:27:52  anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6  in=5018    cache_read=0       code-review-coach\n  The frontier/standard split survives the revert (opus for the finders, sonnet for verify/coach), and caching engages on the Anthropic path too. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY being retained by design is what made all of this possible — the withdrawn 'no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the container' criterion would have made the kill switch a no-op, which is precisely why it was withdrawn.\n\nTHE VOTE (criterion: a real LLM-Review vote produced on the Anthropic path afterwards):\n    voter_voted @ 1785803324.39 = 00:28:44Z\n      change_id   = I58a7822723d10d0fe0c964bdedddbb7b0ae30887\n      revision_id = 5652b147b920163f9ec54a8bd73a326a87783093\n      vote_value  = 1        http_status = 200        decision = PASS        merge = false\n\nAND THIS CLOSES A LOOP I HAD LEFT OPEN. I58a7822723d10... is one of the SAME changes my induced-VOTER_ERROR drill left vote-less at 00:11:14 (it appears by change_id in the recorded VOTER_ERROR lines). It has now received a genuine LLM-Review +1. So the drill's collateral RECOVERED WITHOUT INTERVENTION — the queue/backfill path re-drove the vote-less change exactly as the design intends. I did not /rerun it. That is the recovery half of the drill, evidenced rather than asserted, and it also answers the question the drill's blast radius raised: changes left unvoted by a gate outage do get their vote.\n\nRE-APPLICATION (criterion: the subsequent re-application recorded):\n  00:35:42Z  cp -a /tmp/docker-compose.yml.eb6e-backup docker-compose.yml  -> slot lines restored: 3\n             docker compose up -d --force-recreate review-bot  -> Recreated / Started\n             rebar's resolution back to:\n                 frontier -> bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n                 standard -> bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n                 trivial  -> bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\n             systemctl start rebar-autodeploy.timer -> autodeploy_timer=started, is-active=active\n  The box is left in the SAME state main describes — no hand-edit persists, which is what the runbook insists on ('Do not leave the box hand-edited').\n\nSEQUENCING NOTE, deliberate: I ran this BEFORE the denied-access IAM drill. Breaking Bedrock IAM takes the gate down with no cross-provider fallback by design, so I wanted a PROVEN escape hatch in hand before deliberately creating that condition, rather than discovering the lever's first real exercise was also my only way out."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785803875928860001,"uuid":"85ec18d9-568e-4d51-9c11-4155081572d7"}